{"assets":["/statement-assets/d9664d3aaae51a5f1747e92a854c40980adcd45238e9217e1bebf745062aade1.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2229","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Deconstruction Tree"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A tree with $$$n$$$ nodes fell from the sky along with an initially empty set $$$S$$$. Ecstatic by this unlikely event, you do the following $$$n - 1$$$ times:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" let $$$x$$$ be the leaf with maximum index. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" add $$$x$$$ into $$$S$$$ (note that if $$$x$$$ is already in $$$S$$$ then nothing changes). "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" select any leaf other than $$$x$$$ and remove it from the tree. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Determine the number of distinct sets $$$S$$$ you can make. As the number could be ginormous, output it modulo $$$998\\,244\\,353$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^4$$$). The description of the test cases follows. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each testcase contains an integer $$$n$$$ ($$$2 \\le n \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$) — the size of the tree."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then $$$n - 1$$$ lines follow, each of which contain two integers $$$u$$$ and $$$v$$$ ($$$1 \\le u,v \\le n, u \\ne v$$$), which describe a pair of vertices connected by an edge. It is guaranteed that the given graph is a tree."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$2 \\cdot 10^5$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output the number of distinct sets that can be obtained modulo $$$998\\,244\\,353$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n6\n2\n1 2\n5\n5 1\n5 3\n5 4\n5 2\n7\n7 6\n7 4\n5 7\n1 6\n2 4\n3 5\n10\n10 9\n10 8\n10 7\n10 6\n9 5\n8 4\n7 3\n6 2\n5 1\n4\n2 4\n3 1\n1 4\n4\n1 4\n2 3\n3 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1\n1\n3\n13\n1\n1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For the first testcase, there is only one possible order: $$$1$$$, making the set $$$\\{2\\}$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For the third testcase, the tree looks as follows: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/d9664d3aaae51a5f1747e92a854c40980adcd45238e9217e1bebf745062aade1.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"you can make the sets: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\{3, 6, 7\\}$$$ by removing in the order $$$1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\{3, 4, 6, 7\\}$$$ by removing in the order $$$2, 1, 3, 4, 5, 6$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\{3, 4, 5, 6, 7\\}$$$ by removing in the order $$$2, 3, 1, 4, 5, 6$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It can be proven that these are the only sets obtainable."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"2229E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2229/problem/E"}